        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-661_44104_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="margin: 0 0 8pt; line-height: 107%; font-size: 11pt">Other Charges represents a monthly facility charge.</p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-662_44100_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="margin: 0 0 8pt; line-height: 107%; font-size: 11pt">Southwest Water Authority is a member of McKenzie ElectricCooperative, Inc. and purchases electric service and wheeling services.<span> </span></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-665_44102_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="margin: 0 0 8pt; line-height: 107%; font-size: 11pt">Southwest Water Authority is a preference customer of WAPAand received an allocation of power for one of their water pumping stations inMcKenzie Electric Cooperative, Inc.s service area.<span> </span></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-666_44101_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="margin: 0 0 8pt; line-height: 107%; font-size: 11pt">Western Area Power Administration is a power marketingadministration within the U.S. Department of Energy whose role is to market andtransmit electricity from multi-use water projects to preference customers.</p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-667_44103_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="margin: 0 0 8pt; line-height: 107%; font-size: 11pt">MegaWatt Hours Received and MegaWatt Hours Delivered willequal as represented by the actual delivery.<span> </span>However, due to timing issues, the meter reading used to bill SouthwestWater their wheeling charges is an additional meter used to read and bill usageprior to receipt of Western Area Power Administration transmission deliveryinvoice of actual MegaWatt hours delivered.<span> </span>The wheeling MegaWatt Hours and charges are trued-up annually (in thefollowing period) based on actual receipt and delivery of MegaWatt Hours.</p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1559_44105_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="text-align: left"><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Roboto">The Expenses of Utility column represents the total amount of expenses for regulatory commission expenses. The expenses are not broken out by docket number.</span><br /></p></link:footnote>
    </link:footnoteLink>
</xbrl>